Experiment: To study and execute linux process management commands and use Vi and nano text editors for creating, editing and managing text files in Ubuntu Linux.

Procedure:
(A) Process Management Commands:-
(i) Open terminal in Ubuntu.
(ii) Check running processes - ps
(iii) Display all running processes - ps aux.
(iv) Continually monitor processes - top
(v) Find a process by name - pgrep process_name.
(vi) Terminate a process - kill PID
(vii) Run a process in the background - Command &
(viii) View background jobs - jobs

(B) Using Nano Editor :-
(i) Create / Open a file - nano text.txt.
(ii) Type some text.
(iii) Press Ctrl + O -> Enter to save.
(iv) Press Ctrl + X to exit.

(C) Using Vi Editor:-
(i) Create / Open a file - Vi text.txt
(ii) Press i to enter Insert mode.
(iii) Type your text and press Esc.
(iv) Type - :wq and press enter to save and exit.

Result: Successfully executed linux process management commands and used Vi and Nano Editors to create, edit, save and manage text files in Ubuntu linux.
